ent_hash_method":"tex-environment-body-comments-removed","current_statement_sha256":"sha256:23775549b1a1ec05c3777041d0e9c0518c902f6777abfff8e60cda8817e35664","file":"preprints/A-uniform-Hilbert-transform-estimate-for-Lipschitz-directions-September-25-2026/build/sections/01-introduction.tex","line":17,"producer_hash_method":"atlas-whitespace-normalized-text","producer_statement_sha256":"fe394dffcc781b3f0fff266430947a4b14374012b4354816ce33e8823dc57d33","provenance":{"kind":"computed","pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb","source":"preprints/A-uniform-Hilbert-transform-estimate-for-Lipschitz-directions-September-25-2026/build/sections/01-introduction.tex"},"sha256":"sha256:23775549b1a1ec05c3777041d0e9c0518c902f6777abfff8e60cda8817e35664","url":"https://github.com/openai/math/blob/fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb/preprints/A-uniform-Hilbert-transform-estimate-for-Lipschitz-directions-September-25-2026/build/sections/01-introduction.tex#L17"},"statement_kind":"theorem","text":"\\label{thm:main}\nThere are absolute constants \\(a_*\\in(0,1/2)\\) and \\(C_*<\\infty\\)\nsuch that every Lipschitz field \\(v:\\R^2\\to S^1\\) with\n\\(\\Lip(v)\\le1\\) satisfies\n\\[\n \\sup_{0<\\epsilon<a_*}\n \\norm{H_{v,a_*}^{\\epsilon}f}_{L^2(\\R^2)}\n \\le C_*\\norm{f}_{L^2(\\R^2)}\n \\qquad(f\\in\\mathcal S(\\R^2)).\n\\]\nIts symmetric principal value therefore satisfies\n\\[\n \\norm{H_{v,a_*}f}_2\\le C_*\\norm f_2,\n \\qquad\n \\big|\\{x:|H_{v,a_*}f(x)|>\\lambda\\}\\big|\n \\le C_*^2\\lambda^{-2}\\norm f_2^2\n \\quad(\\lambda>0).\n\\]"}
